  "reason": "The study discusses the limitations and reproducibility of preclinical cancer research, specifically mentioning the inadequacy of animal models as a factor contributing to the low success rate of translating research to clinical success. It reports a quantitative measure of concordance (11% of landmark studies were confirmed) and discusses the challenges of using animal models in drug development. This meets the criteria for including studies that report quantitative measures of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results."
